Project 3 Phase 2 Write Up

How to play the game:
  To play the game you will use the arrow keys to move the plane. Your goal is to collect the rings and avoid any buildings or crash into the ground.

Results of playtesting:
  The results of playtesting was that the player could move around while collecting the rings and photos. Fuel is refilled when collecting the orange rings while points are deducted when collecting the red rings.
  A boost is given when collecting the photos and players are able to see their scores in the top right corner.

4 changes that were made:
  1. I decided to change the theme of the game. Originally the game was more geared towards the fun casual side. You had a funky
     tune that played. But the new theme is more on the darker side. Starting with the title screen we see the game go from the title of Infinite Flyer to Operation 81192. This is significant because it relates
     to a event on April 1st 2001 where a chinese F8 interceptor collided with a US Navy plane. So the theme of the game is centered around that event. Once you start the game you would notice the background is
     a lot less bright, when compared to the original infinite flyer game. You would also notice a slight fog. When it comes to the plane itself, you will see the old chinese flag on each wing of the plane and to
     fit the theme of the plane leaking fuel/gong to crash, I added the element that resembles smoke/fuel leaking at the back of the plane. The background music is also changed into a battlefield sound.

  2. I decided to then add a new dynamic element called photo collectable that would reward the player. The photo collectable element has it's own look, sound, and effect. The look is a photo of a city in china.
     This further fits with the theme where it's saying that the pilot gets the photo and is more motivated to go on. Contrary to the ring, the photo collectable element doesn't give you more points but instead
     it gives you a speed boost for 2 seconds. This rewards the player by essentially giving the player more fuel in the form of time since if the plane can travel more distance in the same amount of time, the 
     more chances it can collect more orange rings to replish it's fuel supply.

  3. Next I decided to add another dynamic element that would harm the player known as danger ring. The danger ring element has it's own looks. sound, and effect. Contrary to what the ring does, the effect of the
     danger rings (red color rings) is to deduct points. If the plane were to fly into them, the player loses 100 points. If the player has no points then flying into the rings would simply have it's effects null.
     This essentially forces the player to avoid these rings making the game harder.

  4. Finally I decided to give meaning to leveling by making the point system differ as you level up. So at first we start at level 0 and it doesn't matter if you collect orange rings or not your points remain zero.
     This causes you to be careful on how you play the game because you have to be alert at the start of the game so that you don't run out of fuel before level 1 where flying into a orange ring will replish your fuel.
     Once you get to level 1 the point system start operating on the equation of (level*200) for close range, (level*100) for medium range, and (level*50) for far range. What this means is that for example if you were
     on level 6 and you fly right into the center of the ring, you would get a +1200 added to your score. If you fly medium range you get a +600 and if you fly far range (aka near the edge of the ring where you just
     so touched it, you will get +300. And so this gives meaning to leveling because each level gives you more points then previous levels so if challenges the player as better players would progress onto the higher
     levels and with that, they get more points. For example, at level 1 you might only get 1000 points total before moving on to level 2, but at level 20, any orange ring you touch would give you a minimum of +1000,
     and so that gives meaning to leveling.
